#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068599 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da0ca17e-50f3-5f67-bb1c-27868f7b4f45" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Cubic Polynomial by a Quadratic Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "a2aac357-23c5-5038-84c6-bc263bd45afa" :question/math-academy-id "e-5143" :question/problem "Determine the quotient and remainder of $6x^3-x^2+3x+1$ divided by $3x^2+x+2.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-1 \\\\  & 3{x}^{2}+x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{3}-\\phantom{0}{x}^{2}+3x+1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-x+1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,3{x}^{2}-x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is ${\\color{blue}2x-1},$ and\n\n- the remainder is ${\\color{red}3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068600 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "525be9c7-af11-506b-be69-444dfc640add" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Polynomials When the Dividend Contains Zero Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "bd9a160c-574e-506e-865c-d08061c75aed" :question/math-academy-id "e-5144" :question/problem "Find the quotient and remainder of the following division problem:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^4 - 7x^2 - x + 8}{x^2 - 1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^3$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:\n\n$$\n2x^4-7x^2-x+8 = 2x^4+{\\color{red}0}x^3-7x^2-x+8\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-5 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x+8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5{x}^{2}-x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,5{x}^{2}+0x+5}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is ${2x^2 - 5},$ and\n\n- the remainder is ${-x+3}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^4 - 7x^2 - x +8}{x^2 - 1} \n= \n2x^2-5 + \\dfrac{-x+3}{x^2-1}.\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^4 - 7x^2 - x +8}{x^2 - 1} \n= \n2x^2-5 - \\dfrac{x-3}{x^2-1}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068660 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76a7314b-4ebf-52eb-b464-97865ea9a81e" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Quartic Polynomial by a Quadratic or Cubic Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "9438b41b-2ad4-5248-881c-cb938b6cf1c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-8932" :question/problem "Find the quotient and remainder of the following division problem:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {5x^4- 2x^3 - 18x^2 + 11x - 13} {5x^2-2x+2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-4 \\\\  & 5{x}^{2}-2x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,5{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}+11x-13\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-20{x}^{2}+11x-13 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,20{x}^{2}+8x-8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n- the quotient is $x^2-4,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $3x-5.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x^4-2x^3-18x^2+11x-13}{5x^2-2x+2}=x^2-4 + \\dfrac{3x-5}{5x^2-2x+2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da0ca17e-50f3-5f67-bb1c-27868f7b4f45" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Cubic Polynomial by a Quadratic Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6da7150-6fe1-54fc-855f-b387232f32e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x - 1" :db/id #edb/r